https://github.com/ceph/s3select/pull/169

arrow >= 24.0.0 removed the arrow::util::span shim in favor of std::span
(GH-48588, apache/arrow#49492), so `#include "arrow/util/span.h"` and
`::arrow::util::span<...>` no longer exist. arrow >= 22.0.0 also switched
InternalFileDecryptor to store encryption keys in arrow::util::SecureString
instead of std::string; the vendored encryption_internal_20.h /
internal_file_decryptor_20.h added by 48-arrow20.patch predate that and
still declare the old (span-based / string-keyed) layout, which happens to
link against the arrow 20-23 build of libparquet (SecureString has the same
layout as std::string) but no longer compiles at all once span.h is gone.

Add a third variant of the two vendored parquet-internal headers
(encryption_internal_24.h / internal_file_decryptor_24.h) that match
verbatim what parquet/encryption/{encryption_internal,internal_file_decryptor}.h
declare in arrow >= 24 (checked against apache-arrow-25.0.1), and select it
via ARROW_VERSION_MAJOR. The ARROW_VERSION_MAJOR >= 20 code path already in
s3select_parquet_intrf.h (constructing InternalFileDecryptor and calling
GetColumn{Meta,Data}DecryptorFactory) has an unchanged signature all the
way through arrow 25.

Separately, arrow 25 added an `allow_short_read` bool parameter to the
DoReadAt() hook that arrow::io::internal::RandomAccessFileConcurrencyWrapper
calls on its CRTP subclass (checked against apache-arrow-25.0.1's
cpp/src/arrow/io/concurrency.h and cpp/src/arrow/io/file.cc). The vendored
arrow::io::ceph::ReadableFile shim in s3select_parquet_intrf.h still
implements the pre-25 two/three-argument overloads, so add the new
parameter to both the declaration and the out-of-line definitions to match;
it isn't forwarded further since the underlying RGW range-read plumbing
already always attempts a full read.
